# Fiber Hooks System

## Available Hooks (8 Total)

1. **OnRoute** - Executes on each route registration
2. **OnName** - Executes when routes are named
3. **OnGroup** - Executes on each group registration
4. **OnGroupName** - Executes when groups are named
5. **OnListen** - Executes during server startup
6. **OnFork** - Executes during process forking
7. **OnShutdown** - Executes after application shutdown
8. **OnMount** - Executes after sub-app mounting

---

## Hook Registration Timing

### ⚠️ CRITICAL: Register hooks BEFORE defining routes

**❌ Incorrect Order:**

```go
app := fiber.New()

// Define routes first
app.Get("/users", getUsers)

// Hook won't capture the route above
app.Hooks().OnRoute(func(r fiber.Route) error {
    log.Printf("Route: %s %s", r.Method, r.Path)
    return nil
})
```

**✅ Correct Order:**

```go
app := fiber.New()

// Register hooks FIRST
app.Hooks().OnRoute(func(r fiber.Route) error {
    log.Printf("Route: %s %s", r.Method, r.Path)
    return nil
})

// Then define routes
app.Get("/users", getUsers) // Will trigger OnRoute hook
```

