## OnMount Hook

### Sub-Application Mounting

```go
// Create main app
main := fiber.New()

// Create sub-app
sub := fiber.New()

sub.Hooks().OnMount(func(parent *fiber.App) error {
    log.Printf("Sub-app mounted to parent")
    // Access parent app configuration
    return nil
})

// Define sub-app routes
sub.Get("/users", getUsers)

// Mount sub-app
main.Mount("/api", sub)

// Routes will be: /api/users
```

**⚠️ Mount-Sensitive Hooks:**

When using `OnRoute`, `OnName`, `OnGroup`, or `OnGroupName` on a sub-app, **paths will include the mount prefix**.

```go
sub := fiber.New()

sub.Hooks().OnRoute(func(r fiber.Route) error {
    log.Printf("Route: %s", r.Path)
    return nil
})

sub.Get("/users", getUsers)

main := fiber.New()
main.Mount("/api/v1", sub)

// Hook will log: "/api/v1/users" (includes mount prefix)
```

